      "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1030894/000103089426000050/cls-20260930.htm",
      "excerpt": "HPS revenue for Q3 2026 increased 70% to approximately $2.3 billion compared to Q3 2025, and accounted for 40% of our total Q3 2026 revenue (Q3 2025 — 44% of our total Q3 2025 revenue). Our HPS revenue for YTD 2026 increased 64% to approximately $5.9 billion compared to YTD 2025, and accounted for 41% of our total YTD 2026 revenue (YTD 2025 — 42% of our total YTD 2025 revenue). HPS revenue growth was driven by program ramps across multiple hyperscaler customers. Compute & Storage end market revenue increased $1,139.0 million (242%) in Q3 2026 compared to Q3 2025 and increased $2,279.7 million (173%) in YTD 2026 compared to YTD 2025, driven by the continued growth in hyperscaler AI compute volumes and strength in our storage programs. ATS segment revenue increased $176.4 million (23%) in Q3 2026 compared to Q3 2025, and increased $244.4 million (10%) in YTD 2026 compared to YTD 2025, primarily due to acceleration in our Capital Equipment business, as well as increased demand in each of our other businesses. We depend on a small number of customers for a substantial portion of our revenue. In the aggregate, our top 10 customers represented 85% of total revenue for Q3 2026 and 84% of total revenue for YTD 2026 (Q3 2025 — 80%; YTD 2025 — 79%). Three customers (all in our CCS segment) individually represented 10% or more of total revenue in Q3 2026 (35%, 17% and 14%) and YTD 2026 (34%, 16% and 15%). Three customers (all in our CCS segment) individually represented 10% or more of total revenue in Q3 2025 (30%, 15% and 14%) and in YTD 2025 (30%, 14% and 12%). Gross profit: The following table shows gross profit and gross margin (gross profit as a percentage of total revenue) for the periods indicated: Three months ended September 30 Nine months ended September 30 2026 2025 2026 2025 Gross profit (in millions) $ 640.8 $ 416.1 $ 1,655.5 $ 1,061.0 Gross margin 11.0 % 13.0 % 11.4 % 12.1 % Gross profit increased by 54% or $224.7 million to $640.8 million in Q3 2026 compared to Q3 2025 and increased by 56% or $594.5 million to $1,655.5 million in YTD 2026 compared to YTD 2025, primarily driven by our strong revenue growth. Gross margin decreased to 11.0% in Q3 2026 from 13.0% in Q3 2025 and decreased to 11.4% in YTD 2026 from 12.1% in YTD 2025. Both gross profit and gross margin were negatively impacted by the unfavorable changes in the fair value adjustments (TRS FVAs) related to our total return swap agreement (TRS Agreement) recorded in cost of sales ($0.9 million loss in Q3 2026 compared to $48.5 million gain in Q3 2025; $40.0 million gain in YTD 2026 compared to $81.6 million gain in YTD 2025), as well as mix dynamics in our CCS business.",
